The Harlequins are the builders of the Strider and the organizers of the pilgrimage. The Party holds a stolen invitation to one such pilgrimage, dated for a Saturday.

The strider under construction at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], where the Party's pilgrimage was held, is their work: a platform on eight legs with buildings on top, still ringed with scaffolding when the guests began to arrive.

On the night of the Ragged Roost pilgrimage the Harlequins worked the party in red-and-green pinstriped shirts, bell-capped masks whose shadow hid the line of the neck, and gloves. Two sat at a table at the head of the line, one taking invitations, the other handing out plain white masks. Others walked the street with platters of champagne and hors d'oeuvres, or ran the attractions, or fetched the smaller ones out of a train to mop the arena floor after a fight.

The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] is the strider the Harlequins raised at Ragged Roost, still unfinished when the guests arrived.
